I wake up to the loud sound of the rain.
The rain is hitting heavily against my window.
I get up and look out the window.
Today Mumbai's sky has become completely grey.
Today is my birthday.
I have officially turned thirty-two today.
This is my very first birthday away from home.
I remember the day I arrived here in January.
I came to Mumbai for my new job.
At that time, this city was completely dry.
But now this monsoon has completely changed the streets.
A lot of water has gathered everywhere.
The trees by the street have become very lush green.
I never saw such intense rain in Mexico.
But I really like this fierce weather.
I have fallen in love with this monsoon.
This is a perfect morning for my thirty-second birthday.
